{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The smart plug feels like a useful next step because it would add voice control to a lamp alongside my Alexa-enabled entertainment devices.",
    "The Echo Show 8 fits my interest in connected-home equipment while adding a screen for household information and occasional video calls."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The HD and previous-generation Fire TV Sticks repeat something my 4K Stick and Fire TV television already provide, without a clear improvement.",
    "Earbuds and a tablet do not address a current need just because they are electronics; memory cards also need a specific use and confirmed compatibility before I would choose them.",
    "The Echo Dots and Show 5 interest me, but I would choose the Show 8 for its larger screen rather than buy several devices for overlapping purposes."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Fire TV purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest more streaming players, even though that need is already covered.",
    "My interest in connected electronics seems to have been stretched into an interest in unrelated personal devices such as earbuds and tablets."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "What matters now is whether a device adds a useful capability to what I already have, rather than repeating an existing function.",
    "Several Alexa devices can appeal to me while still being alternatives to one another; this time I prefer one larger display.",
    "My camera purchases do not establish that I need more storage or that these particular memory cards would work with my equipment."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my interest in an Alexa-connected home but give too little weight to existing equipment, overlapping functions, and a concrete current need."
}"}
